{"id": 35, "ts": 1780627037.641086, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I concur with Sarah\u2019s move to Candidate\u202fC. The evidence we have shows C is 100\u202f% reliable, creates a positive crew atmosphere, stays calm in a crisis, makes correct decisions quickly, and understands complicated technology\u2014covering reliability, stress resilience, decision quality, and technical competence. While C\u2019s difficulty communicating ideas and egocentric attitude are concerns, the positive crew atmosphere suggests those traits have not yet translated into unsafe teamwork. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB still lacks any concrete evidence of crew cooperation, and the noted grumpiness and pretentious tone remain unresolved risks. Before we lock in a final hire, we should still surface the remaining profiles\u2014particularly Candidate\u202fA\u2019s leadership and anticipation versus his show\u2011off reputation and resistance to new ideas, and Candidate\u202fD\u2019s strong problem\u2011solving and responsibility against his hot temper and know\u2011it\u2011all perception\u2014to ensure we haven\u2019t overlooked a better overall fit. For now, my provisional recommendation is Candidate\u202fC."}
